-- title:
--   Independence of powers of E₄E₆/Δ mod q over X₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic $q$, and let $M$ be a positive integer with $M \ge 5$ and $q \nmid M$. Write $K_0 =$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) $\kappa\,M$ for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\kappa(\!(X)\!)$ over $\kappa$ generated by the family `intFormRatiosC` $\kappa$ $\Gamma_1(M)$, and let $\bar g \in \kappa(\!(X)\!)$ be the quotient
--   $$\bar g = \frac{\bigl(1 + \sum_{n \ge 1} 240\,\sigma_3(n)X^n\bigr)\bigl(1 - \sum_{n \ge 1} 504\,\sigma_5(n)X^n\bigr)}{X\prod_{n \ge 1}(1 - X^{n})^{24}},$$
--   each factor being the image in $\kappa(\!(X)\!)$, coefficientwise via $\mathbb{Z} \to \kappa$, of the indicated integral power series (the denominator being $X$ times the $24$th power of [`ModularCurve.etaProd`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L119)). Then for any family $e : \mathrm{Fin}\,((q-1)/2) \to \kappa(\!(X)\!)$ with every $e_i \in K_0$, the relation $\sum_{i} e_i\,\bar g^{\,i} = 0$ forces $e_i = 0$ for all $i$. Equivalently, $1, \bar g, \dots, \bar g^{(q-3)/2}$ are linearly independent over $K_0$.
--
--   The statement expresses, in $q$-expansion form, that the reduction modulo $q$ of $E_4E_6/\Delta$ generates a Kummer-type extension of degree at least $(q-1)/2$ over the function field of $X_1(M)$ in characteristic $q$; it rests on the fact that the inverse of an integral weight-one form with non-zero reduction is a Kummer generator of exponent $q-1$ for the Igusa covering. It is used in the full-level analysis of the Igusa function field, in particular by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isKummerGenerator_eisensteinRatio_and_igusaFunctionField_eq_xHFunctionFieldC_levelH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isKummerGenerator_eisensteinRatio_and_igusaFunctionField_eq_xHFunctionFieldC_levelH) and the accompanying independence and descent statements.
-- source:
